data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with `nint` and `nuint` into a `Span`.**

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[4];
```

Both work without any `unsafe` context — `stackalloc` into a `Span<T>` is safe. On this 64-bit system each element is 8 bytes. The only caveat is that `sizeof(nint)` still requires an `unsafe` block since `nint`/`nuint` don't have a compile-time-fixed size.
